## Sources

<One bullet per source actually cited above, every bib key verifiable in
`docs/references/references.bib`. Exact format, one line each:>

```
- `bibkey` — Author(s) (Year), "Title," *Venue*. doi:10.xxxx/xxxxx
- `bibkey` — Author(s) (Year), "Title," *Venue*. url:https://example.com/paper
- `bibkey` — Author(s) (Year), "Title," *Venue*. file-only (docs/references/bibkey.pdf)
```

Rules for this section:
- Exactly one bullet per bib key, no grouping multiple keys on one line.
- The locator after the final period is always exactly one of `doi:<doi>`,
  `url:<url>`, or `file-only (docs/references/<bibkey>.pdf)` — matching
  whichever field the bib entry actually carries preferentially (DOI >
  URL > file-only per `.friday/active/harness/roles/researcher.md` "Tooling").
- No footnote-style `[1]`/`[2]` numbering and no markdown links to the
  `.bib` file itself — the bib key in backticks is the only identifier
  needed; `.friday/active/harness/tools/verify_references.py` and
  `.friday/active/harness/tools/lint_research_memo.py` both key off this exact shape.
